EGG-SR sits below GenSR (5.0) because GenSR has broader empirical validation on SRBench. It sits around FineScope (4.67) and SymLight (5.5) in terms of the overclaim-plus-narrow-evaluation pattern. The theoretical contributions pull it up slightly, but the factual inaccuracy in the DRL claim and the trigonometric-only evaluation pull it down. I place it at 4.5—below the borderline, primarily because the evaluation scope doesn't support the breadth of the claims, and the paper contains a directly false statement about DRL performance.

