SCaSML sits between the 5.5 anchors (inference-time scaling with compute-fairness concerns) and the 6.5 anchor (multifidelity control variate with cleaner evaluation). Its theoretical contribution (Theorem 2.5, Corollary 2.6) is genuine and the method works consistently, but the unverified strong assumption and missing fixed-budget comparison in the main text prevent it from scoring higher. It is below Frozen-PINN (7.0) due to weaker empirical methodology and overclaiming, and well above MOFS (2.5) which lacks both theory and rigorous evaluation.

