The paper is clearly above the low-scoring anchors (IBNorm at 4.0, ALoRA at 3.5) where theoretical flaws were more severe or experiments were more limited. It sits in the same band as mtLoRA (5.50) and QuestA (6.0)—both accepted as posters with clean methods, strong empirical results, and imperfect theoretical sections. This paper has a more significant theoretical misrepresentation than QuestA (which merely had an "unnecessary" theory section), but also has a more coherent narrative arc and a more comprehensive evaluation than mtLoRA. Below the high-scoring anchors (Command-V at 7.0) which had cleaner contributions without the overclaiming issues.

