Our paper sits between the RO-HNN/SPS-GAN cluster (4.0, rejected) and IGNS (4.5, accepted poster). It has stronger empirical evidence than RO-HNN (the comprehensive Table 2 sweep and energy visualization) but shares similar weaknesses (overclaimed framing, missing baselines, limited novelty from combining existing methods). The missing HNN baseline and the "smaller models" overclaim are significant but not fatal—the paper still demonstrates genuine and well-quantified advantages for structure-preserving approaches.

